    "S1": {
      "caption_label": "TABLE S1",
      "caption_title": "REDSEA MATCHING AND CELL RETENTION AUDIT",
      "caption": "Table S1. REDSEA matching and cell retention audit.",
      "note": "Counts are pooled across the eight B004 regions. Processed counts refer to segmentation objects retained in the processed H5ADs. Matched counts include objects accepted by directed nearest-neighbor matching within 10 source-coordinate units after swapping the reference x and y coordinates. Multiple segmentation objects could match the same reference cell. Shared objects had the same CellID within a region and unchanged coordinates. Before-only and after-only counts were based on CellID, not saved row indices. Paired F1 evaluation also required an accepted match to the same reference cell and label in both conditions, so the shared-ID column is not its final scoring denominator. These counts describe retention and matching, not segmentation-boundary accuracy.",
      "rows_including_header": 7,
      "columns": 6,
      "cell_order_sha256": "4275ec628067f81164f828339b11bd18b9006f01ad4b3865ad26d5c64b8264e0",
