      "caption": "Table S12a. GPT-6 Astra cross-model support calibration.",
      "note": "ECE is expected calibration error. Lower scores are better. Metrics give equal weight to the two test regions and use only evaluation clusters held out by the cluster-hash split, rather than the full benchmark population. Development and evaluation use nonoverlapping clusters and regions. Cross-model support has a denominator of four. This retrospective within-donor calibration measures reference agreement, not repeatability, an individual model’s confidence or biological certainty.",
